messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 363171983 and 336390092? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 363171983 and 336390092, we can follow these steps:.\n\n1. Align the numbers by their place values, making sure that the ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, etc., are in the same columns.\n2. Add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place).\n3. If the sum of the digits in any column is greater than 9, carry over the extra digit to the next column to the left.\n4. Continue adding the digits in each column, including any carried-over digits, until you reach the leftmost column (the thousands place).\n\nLet's perform the addition:.\n\n```.\n  363171983.\n+ 336390092.\n----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n3 + 2 = 5.\n\nNext column (the tens place):.\n\n8 + 9 = 17 (write down 7 and carry over 1).\n\nNext column (the hundreds place):.\n\n1 + 0 + 1 (carried over) = 2.\n\nNext column (the thousands place):.\n\n9 + 0 + 1 (carried over) = 10 (write down 0 and carry over 1).\n\nNext column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carried over) = 5.\n\nNext column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n7 + 6 + 1 (carried over) = 14 (write down 4 and carry over 1).\n\nNext column (the millions place):.\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carried over) = 5.\n\nFinally, the leftmost column (the ten-millions place):.\n\n3 + 3 = 6. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
